    <unit id="1" name="BasicTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Basic</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="2" name="BasicDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Click DatePicker, and then we could select or input a date in panel.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="3" name="SwitchableTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Switchable picker</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="4" name="SwitchableDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Switch between TimePicker and DatePicker modes from a single selector.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="5" name="BindingTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>SelectedDateTime binding</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="6" name="BindingDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>SelectedDateTime, RangeStartSelectedDate, and RangeEndSelectedDate synchronize with the ViewModel without explicitly setting Binding Mode=TwoWay.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="7" name="PickerDisplayDateTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Popup display date</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="8" name="PickerDisplayDateDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Open the popup panel at a specific display date without committing a selected value.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="9" name="MinMaxTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Date range limits</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="10" name="MinMaxDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Use MinDate and MaxDate to limit the selectable date range. Boundary dates are included.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="11" name="RangePickerTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Range Picker</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="12" name="RangePickerDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>Set range picker type by picker prop.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="13" name="NeedConfirmTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Need Confirm</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="14" name="NeedConfirmDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>DatePicker will automatically determine whether to show a confirm button according to the picker property. You can also set the needConfirm property to determine whether to show a confirm button. When needConfirm is set, the user must click the confirm button to complete the selection. Otherwise, the selection will be submitted when the picker loses focus or selects a date.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="15" name="ChooseTimeTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Choose Time</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="16" name="ChooseTimeDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>This property provides an additional time selection. When showTime is an Object, its properties will be passed on to the built-in TimePicker.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="17" name="DisabledTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Disabled</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="18" name="DisabledDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>A disabled state of the DatePicker. You can also set as array to disable one of input.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="19" name="ThreeSizesTitle">
      <segment>
        <source>Three Sizes</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="20" name="ThreeSizesDescription">
      <segment>
        <source>The input box comes in three sizes: small, middle and large. The middle size will be used if size is omitted.</source>
      </segment>
    </unit>
